  "scientific_question": "Among CA1 pyramidal neurons already exposed to nearby reactive astrocytes, does the fraction that also lie in a lymphocyte-positive microenvironment predict worse memory decline better than the current simpler immune-contact features?",
  "approach": "Assign cells to CA1 using annotation polygons after dividing polygon coordinates by 16, then identify CA1 Pyramidal Neuron, Reactive Astrocyte, and Lymphocyte centroids. For each CA1 pyramidal neuron, mark reactive-astro exposure if at least one Reactive Astrocyte lies within 25 um. Among those exposed pyramidal neurons, count Lymphocytes within 25 um and compute the donor-level score as the fraction of reactive-astro-exposed pyramidal neurons meeting the chosen lymphocyte-count threshold.",
  "variations": [
    {
      "name": "candidate_variant_a",
      "description": "Fraction of CA1 reactive-astro-exposed pyramidal neurons with at least 1 lymphocyte within 25 um."
    },
    {
      "name": "candidate_variant_b",
      "description": "Fraction of CA1 reactive-astro-exposed pyramidal neurons with at least 2 lymphocytes within 25 um."
    }
  ],
  "baseline_variation": "candidate_variant_a",
  "notes": "Use centroid-to-centroid distances only; convert 25 um to pixels with slide-specific MPP from the paired SVS metadata if available. Keep denominator restricted to CA1 pyramidal neurons that have at least one Reactive Astrocyte within 25 um. If CA1 is missing or the donor has zero reactive-astro-exposed CA1 pyramidal neurons, return NaN rather than forcing 0. Handle label matching exactly as stored in ClassificationNode.",
  "rationale": "Rounds 7 and 8 both improved the panel by adding lymphocyte-associated CA1 reactive-astro signals, suggesting the inflammatory niche is real, but the current features are mostly binary presence measures on broader denominators. The next clean test is to condition on the reactive-astro-exposed pyramidal subset and ask whether lymphocyte enrichment within that subset is a sharper, potentially replaceable-or-additive biomarker than the existing contact/triad terms."
